<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-100 mb-6">Plugins</h1>

<p class="text-zinc-400 mb-6">
  Plugins extend botster with custom behavior. They're Lua scripts loaded at hub startup.
</p>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-200 mt-8 mb-3">Plugin location</h2>
<p class="text-zinc-400 mb-4">
  Place plugins in the <code class="text-zinc-300 bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">plugins/</code>
  directory at either level:
</p>
<pre class="bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-zinc-300 font-mono overflow-x-auto mb-6"><code>~/.botster/plugins/my-plugin/init.lua        # Device-level (all repos)
your-repo/.botster/plugins/my-plugin/init.lua # Repo-level (this repo only)</code></pre>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-200 mt-8 mb-3">Plugin structure</h2>
<p class="text-zinc-400 mb-4">
  Each plugin is a directory with an <code class="text-zinc-300 bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">init.lua</code> entry point.
  Other filenames are plugin-owned; require them from <code class="text-zinc-300 bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">init.lua</code>.
</p>
<pre class="bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-zinc-300 font-mono overflow-x-auto mb-6"><code>plugins/
  my-plugin/
    init.lua       # Entry point, loaded at startup
    web_layout.lua # Optional web surface module
    tui/
      status.lua   # Optional TUI extension module</code></pre>

<p class="text-zinc-400 mb-4">
  TUI client files are declared in the comment header of <code class="text-zinc-300 bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">init.lua</code>
  so the TUI can load only client-safe code:
</p>
<pre class="bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-zinc-300 font-mono overflow-x-auto mb-6"><code>-- @tui tui/status.lua
local web_layout = require("web_layout")</code></pre>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-200 mt-8 mb-3">Plugin surfaces</h2>
<p class="text-zinc-400 mb-4">
  Plugins can register browser surfaces and ask core to place them in navigation. Icon names come from the vendored Heroicons mini set under
  <code class="text-zinc-300 bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">app/assets/svg/icons/heroicons/mini</code>, so use the Heroicon filename without
  <code class="text-zinc-300 bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">.svg</code>.
</p>
<pre class="bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-zinc-300 font-mono overflow-x-auto mb-6"><code>surfaces.register("vault", {
  label = "Vault",
  icon = "book-open",
  nav = { section = "workspace", order = 25 },
  routes = {
    { path = "/", render = vault_home },
    { path = "/sessions/:session_uuid", render = vault_session },
  },
})</code></pre>
<p class="text-zinc-400 mb-4">
  Plugin-owned sessions can stay out of the normal workspace sidebar while remaining visible inside the plugin surface:
</p>
<pre class="bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-zinc-300 font-mono overflow-x-auto mb-6"><code>ui.session_list{
  visibility = "plugin",
  owner_plugin = "vault",
  surface = "vault",
}

ui.session_terminal{
  session_uuid = state.params.session_uuid,
  back = ctx.path("/"),
}</code></pre>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-200 mt-8 mb-3">Load order</h2>
<p class="text-zinc-400">
  Plugins are loaded in alphabetical order. Device-level plugins load first, then repo-level.
  Repo plugins override device plugins with the same name.
  Plugins support hot reload &mdash; changes take effect without restarting the hub.
</p>
